<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Achalpur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ellichpur, Elichpur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Achalpur, historically Ellichpur, is a town in the Amravati district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It was the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berar">Berar</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> and the Imad Shahi sultans of Berar, who ruled from it and the nearby fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gawilgarh">Gawilgarh</a>, and it remained the seat of the Mughal province of Berar. Its importance declined after the 18th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/achalpur.jpg" alt="Achalpur" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anubarto · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narrow_guage_train_%27Shakuntala%27_at_Achalpur_Railway_station.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
